 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** The complexity is dominated by the number of texture samples per pixel. The 17-tap box blur and cross-shaped bloom require a fixed number of samples (17 and 5 respectively) per pixel, making the time complexity $O(1)$ with respect to scene complexity but dependent on the resolution [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** The method requires storage for the scene texture, the output buffer, and temporary buffers for bloom and blur passes. The memory usage is proportional to the screen resolution [S1, unofficial].
