 *   **Scaling:** The method scales with screen resolution. The blur and bloom radii are defined in texel space, ensuring consistent visual appearance across different resolutions [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:** Allows for complex aesthetic effects (vignette, bloom, refraction) without modifying the volume rendering pipeline. Efficient for real-time applications [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:** Limited to screen-space effects; cannot account for occlusion or lighting interactions that occur outside the visible screen area. The specific implementation details (e.g., blur taps, bloom weights) are hardcoded and may not be optimal for all scenes [S1, unofficial].
